WEBVTT

c1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.075
Your phone's glass

c2
00:00:01.075 --> 00:00:02.000
feels solid,

c3
00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:02.875
but just under

c4
00:00:02.875 --> 00:00:03.300
it is an

c5
00:00:03.300 --> 00:00:04.300
invisible grid,

c6
00:00:04.300 --> 00:00:05.225
listening for your

c7
00:00:05.225 --> 00:00:05.875
finger.

c8
00:00:05.875 --> 00:00:06.675
Thin lines of

c9
00:00:06.675 --> 00:00:08.025
transparent conductor run

c10
00:00:08.025 --> 00:00:09.325
across in rows,

c11
00:00:09.325 --> 00:00:09.950
and down in

c12
00:00:09.950 --> 00:00:10.800
columns,

c13
00:00:10.800 --> 00:00:11.975
crossing without ever

c14
00:00:11.975 --> 00:00:12.600
touching.

c15
00:00:12.600 --> 00:00:13.600
Every crossing is

c16
00:00:13.600 --> 00:00:15.200
a tiny capacitor.

c17
00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:16.100
The chip pulses

c18
00:00:16.100 --> 00:00:16.825
one line at

c19
00:00:16.825 --> 00:00:17.475
a time,

c20
00:00:17.475 --> 00:00:18.550
and measures every

c21
00:00:18.550 --> 00:00:19.250
crossing.

c22
00:00:19.250 --> 00:00:20.350
Your finger conducts

c23
00:00:20.350 --> 00:00:21.475
electricity,

c24
00:00:21.475 --> 00:00:22.275
so it steals

c25
00:00:22.275 --> 00:00:22.800
a little of

c26
00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:23.700
that field,

c27
00:00:23.700 --> 00:00:24.350
and the signal

c28
00:00:24.350 --> 00:00:25.125
at that crossing

c29
00:00:25.125 --> 00:00:25.825
drops.

c30
00:00:25.825 --> 00:00:26.625
The chip finds

c31
00:00:26.625 --> 00:00:27.300
where the signal

c32
00:00:27.300 --> 00:00:27.975
dropped,

c33
00:00:27.975 --> 00:00:28.525
and that is

c34
00:00:28.525 --> 00:00:29.250
where you touched.

